following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-19T18:01:06Z","updated_at":"2022-07-19T18:01:06Z","body":"My observations:\r\n1. dis.opmap['LOAD_CONST']\r\ncpython: 100\r\nrustpython: AttributeError: module 'dis' has no attribute 'opmap'\r\n2. dis.EXTENDED_ARG\r\ncpython: 144\r\nrustpython: AttributeError: module 'dis' has no attribute 'EXTENDED_ARG'\r\n\r\n3. dis._unpack_opargs(100)\r\ncpython: <generator object _unpack_opargs at 0x7f465322fde0>\r\nrustpython: AttributeError: module 'dis' has no attribute '_unpack_opargs'\r\n\r\nThese are only relevant to [#3863](https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/pull/3863)\r\n\r\nAdditionally:\r\ndir(dis) in cpython\r\n['BINARY_OP', 'Bytecode', 'CACHE', 'COMPILER_FLAG_NAMES', 'EXTENDED_ARG', 'FORMAT_VALUE', 'FORMAT_VALUE_CONVERTERS', 'FOR_ITER', 'HAVE_ARGUMENT', 'Instruction', 'JUMP_BACKWARD', 'LOAD_ATTR', 'LOAD_CONST', 'LOAD_GLOBAL', 'MAKE_FUNCTION', 'MAKE_FUNCTION_FLAGS', 'Positions', 'UNKNOWN', '_ExceptionTableEntry', '_INT_BITS', '_INT_OVERFLOW', '_Instruction', '_OPARG_WIDTH', '_OPNAME_WIDTH', '_Unknown', '__all__', '__builtins__', '__cached__', '__doc__', '__file__', '__loader__', '__name__', '__package__', '__spec__', '_all_opmap', '_all_opname', '_cache_format', '_deoptop', '_disassemble_bytes', '_disassemble_recursive', '_disassemble_str', '_empty_slot', '_find_imports', '_find_store_names', '_format_code_info', '_get_code_array', '_get_code_object', '_get_const_info', '_get_const_value', '_get_instructions_bytes', '_get_name_info', '_have_code', '_inline_cache_entries', '_is_backward_jump', '_nb_ops', '_specializations', '_specialized_instructions', '_test', '_try_compile', '_unpack_opargs', 'cmp_op', 'code_info', 'collections', 'deoptmap', 'dis', 'disassemble', 'disco', 'distb', 'findlabels', 'findlinestarts', 'get_instructions', 'hasarg', 'hascompare', 'hasconst', 'hasexc', 'hasfree', 'hasjabs', 'hasjrel', 'haslocal', 'hasname', 'io', 'opmap', 'opname', 'parse_exception_table', 'parse_varint', 'pretty_flags', 'show_code', 'spec_op', 'specialized', 'stack_effect', 'sys', 'types']\r\n2. rustpython:\r\n ['COMPILER_FLAG_NAMES', '__builtins__', '__cached__', '__doc__', '__file__', '__loader__', '__name__', '__package__', '__spec__', '_test', 'dis', 'disassemble']\r\n\r\nSo how do we approach this problem? Module finder needs _unpack_opargs, EXTENDED_ARG and opmap, if these gets implemented in dis module, requirement of this PR gets fulfilled right? @youknowone \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1189392760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1189835322","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846#issuecomment-1189835322","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846","id":1189835322,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec5G63I6","user":{"login":"youknowone","id":69878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5ODc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone","html_url":"https://github.com/youknowone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-20T05:09:22Z","updated_at":"2022-07-20T05:09:22Z","body":"yes, I think so. another small part is being ready to be not disappointed even when adding them doesn't fix the module.\r\n\r\nyou even don't need to add all of them  in single PR.\r\nwe value and encourage every progressing step (without regression).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1189835322/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1189945136","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846#issuecomment-1189945136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846","id":1189945136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec5G7R8w","user":{"login":"itsankitkp","id":93041495,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYuzVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93041495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp","html_url":"https://github.com/itsankitkp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gi