gs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-20T17:23:32Z","updated_at":"2022-07-20T17:23:32Z","body":"A quick question, how do we all translate python libraries? I get that c code is translated into equivalent rust code but what should be done for the Python code?\r\nFor Python code depending on instruction, rustpython equivalent would need to skip out unimplemented piece but for purely python library (think opcode.py, just hard coded values of opcodes), do we need to translate _something_ or code is practically same as cpython (python) library?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1190551394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1191841449","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846#issuecomment-1191841449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846","id":1191841449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec5HCg6p","user":{"login":"youknowone","id":69878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5ODc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone","html_url":"https://github.com/youknowone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youknowone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-21T19:12:45Z","updated_at":"2022-07-21T19:12:45Z","body":"Ideally, we run the same code.\r\nBut for opcodes, yes, as you described, it cannot be fully compatible. bytecodes are even not compatible between each cpython versions.\r\nWhen I looked in modulefinder a little bit, it only uses a few (probably stable) opcodes. I wish we also has that amount of stability, but I don't know we are or not.\r\n\r\nI don't expect you to translate python code to python code to run it. If you found it is not working, we will accept we cannot run it for now, and try to fix our compiler or vm later.\r\nBut even if it happens, we will get a few new `dis` module features during the journey.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1191841449/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/comments/1193339182","html_url":"https://github.com/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846#issuecomment-1193339182","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RustPython/RustPython/issues/3846","id":1193339182,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCA8Bec5HIOku","user":{"login":"itsankitkp","id":93041495,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYuzVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93041495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp","html_url":"https://github.com/itsankitkp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itsankitkp/followers","following_url":"https:/